Third-party attribution (summary)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The OpenPhonex Gateway depends on third-party components at runtime. None of the
copyleft components below are bundled, forked, modified, or redistributed by
this project; they are obtained by the operator from their respective upstreams.
See THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md for the full enumeration and license texts.

  - faster-whisper (MIT) — optional local STT adapter
  - numpy (BSD-3-Clause) — optional PCM resample helper for local models
  - Piper (MIT) — optional local TTS engine (invoked as an external binary)
  - Kokoro (Apache-2.0) — optional local TTS engine
  - websocket-client (Apache-2.0) — provider streaming transport
  - ffmpeg (LGPL/GPL) — NOT bundled; invoked as an external binary if present

The self-host stack additionally runs the following components as separate
container images / pip packages obtained by the operator directly from their
upstreams (none are bundled or redistributed by this repository): LiveKit
server, LiveKit SIP, and the livekit-agents framework with its provider
plugins (Apache-2.0), and Redis (obtained by the operator from the official
upstream image under its own license).

